    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "11dade61_92ab3d65",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/usb_console.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 24,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000407
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-07T19:04:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The remaining RAM space of the boards which have CONFIG_USB_CONSOLE enabled:\n  stm32f446e-eval 120444\n  twinkie 4620\n  polyberry 118780\n  pdeval-stm32f072 6556\n  tigertail 7068\n  servo_micro 3956\n  discovery-stm32f072 8732\n  sweetberry 114540\n  hammer 3660 (RO), 656 (RW)\n  servo_v4 2336\n\nChanging it to 128 bytes may drop too many chars and the interactive console may become useless. Each printf call is now async, not longer a blocking call. So the buffer grows faster. For example, the gpioget command returns a 1029-byte result, so 2048-byte is picked here.",
      "parentUuid": "87d69b92_3b224a89",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 24,
        "endChar": 48
